  {
    "episode_id": 96064,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96064.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Sure. Well, yeah, I'm actually one of the few members of Congress that actually has served on the border and worked there. And let me just say I was there last week. And it's the worst I've ever seen it. You know, we have had ebbs and flows on our southern border. When I first came into Congress in 2019, we had a crisis on our southern border. President Trump worked very hard to secure the funding to build the wall, to develop the remain in Mexico policy, and to deport people using his Title 42 authority to deport people. And using those, he actually created the most secure border that we had had in a generation. And he handed that to President Biden, who on day one, day one of his presidency, President Biden got rid of the Remain in Mexico policy, stopped building the wall, and stopped reporting. And those three decisions that President Biden implemented on the very first day of his presidency have rendered the least secure border we have seen in a generation. And just a few hours ago, we found out that our numbers, the number of people arrested on the southern border by border patrol in the month of September was three times higher than it has ever been before in the history of our country.",
