  },
  {
    "episode_id": 96064,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96064.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Sure. Well, I think it's important to understand that the south of the Rio Grande is controlled by the drug cartels. Every square inch is controlled by the cartels. And they are running drug smuggling, they're trafficking in sex trafficking, and they're doing a human smuggling operation. And what they have done, these cartels, they advertise on television in the northern triangle countries, right? So El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, they're advertising on television, they're charging between $4,000 and $6,000 per person to smuggle them from these northern trial countries up into Mexico, and then deliver them to Border Patrol. And in fact, the cartels ask for payment based on when they deliver a human being to border patrol. And so the Biden administration has turned border patrol from a patrol into a border processing unit. And so they just process, and then who are they processing? Well, they're processing these people who are human trafficking victims, but they're also helping the cartels deliver their product because if the cartel gets it to the border patrol, then give them a bus ticket, give them a plane ticket, take them anywhere in the country they want to go. I speak decent Spanish. I spoke to several people, and they were telling me, hey, I want to go see my aunt in Nebraska, who paid the cartels to get me smuggled up here. I'm going to go see family in Florida. I'm going to go see family in New Jersey. I'm going to go see family in Portland. So they all have a place they want to go, and they know that if they get to Border Patrol, when we get three hot meals, they're going to get a shower, they're going to get medical, and they're going to get a bus ticket in a couple of weeks to go wherever they want to go. And so the Biden administration, their rhetoric, President Biden's rhetoric, if I want to welcome you in and give you free healthcare, the cartels are exploiting that language to then get more people to make this dangerous journey to pay more money at the cartels. So President Biden has turned the Border Patrol into an extension of the cartels. And furthermore, he's made it easier for the cartels to prey on these people and to get them to pay money and make this dangerous journey to the North.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The south of the Rio Grande is controlled by drug cartels.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
